    area: 5, 7, or 15 [observed]
    bbox: square, observed 4x4 / 5x5 / 9x9
    connectivity: 8-connected, may be 4-disconnected internally
    symmetry: REQUIRED; motif is symmetric across one diagonal of its square bbox
    direction: the occupied endpoint of the symmetry diagonal points to the same grid corner as the triangle
    shape_style: sparse diagonal-symmetric motif matching the original examples, not an asymmetric arrow/random blob
  corner_marker:
    desc: exactly 1 grid corner cell is non-bg; indicates triangle corner
    color: any non-bg, must differ from motif color
    placement: must be the corner pointed to by the motif's occupied diagonal endpoint
  controls:
    desc: singleton non-bg pixels outside the motif, each a separate 8-connected component
    total: 3-6 (including corner marker); triangle_side = total - 1
    fill_color: the unique non-corner control color appearing >=2 times; differs from motif color
    fill_count: 2-3 non-corner pixels of fill_color
    distractors: 0-3 non-corner singletons, each a unique color appearing once; may equal motif color or corner color
    placement: no control pixel is 8-adjacent to the motif; Chebyshev distance >=2
  triangle:
    side: 2-5 (= number of non-corner controls)
    corner: same as motif direction
    rule: fill all cells where (dist_to_corner_row + dist_to_corner_col) < side
    pixels: side*(side+1)/2
    must not overlap motif
  output_rule: clear all controls, redraw motif, paint corner triangle in fill_color

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size (H,W) in ranges.
    2. Pick triangle side S in [2,5]. Choose fill_color and motif_color (distinct, both non-bg).
    3. Sample one of the original sparse square diagonal-symmetric motif
       templates (4x4 area 5/7, 5x5 area 7, or 9x9 area 15) and apply
       rotations/flips. Determine the corner from the occupied endpoint of the
       motif symmetry diagonal (TL/TR/BL/BR).
    4. Paint the S*(S+1)/2 triangle at that motif-pointed corner in fill_color.
       Place the motif so it does not overlap or 8-touch the triangle region.
       This is the output.
    5. Derive input from output -- remove triangle, add controls:
       a. Place corner marker pixel at the chosen corner in a color != motif_color.
       b. Place S non-corner singleton control pixels on bg cells not 8-adjacent to motif:
          exactly fill_count (2-3) use fill_color, remainder (S - fill_count) use
          distinct distractor colors (each unique, any non-bg color).

